<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02112</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>fb8031ac-e8cf-4631-83f6-d99794187a1a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="_5c4d70dc-e487-45ef-b54c-4b2011eccc9d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">The expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> represents the cost to purchase tickets for a concert, where <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the number of tickets. A group of friends paid $79.25 for tickets. How many tickets were bought?</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00004">6 tickets</para>
          <para id="para-00005">8 tickets</para>
          <para id="para-00006">10 tickets</para>
          <para id="para-00007">12 tickets</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00008">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.1.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">The correct answer is 8 tickets.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fbee7c79-87a0-445a-a892-cc8b898f7e73" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00010">Use the following scenario to answer questions 2 – 4.</para>
          <para id="para-00011"><quote id="quote-00001">A model rocket is launched from a launchpad. The function modeling the height of the rocket, in feet, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds after being launched is shown.</quote></para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00013">Which equation would you solve to find the time at which the rocket hits the ground?</para>
          <para id="para-00014">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00019">Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00020">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="af0f6d88-afdc-49c8-8cdb-39521ee2e593" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00021">Use a non-graphing method to find the solution to the previous equation to determine the time that has passed when the rocket hits the ground.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00023">2 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00024">3 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00025">4 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00026">5 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00027">Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00028">The correct answer is 4 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_77177ead-21bf-47d5-8c05-3f3b97d87f3e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00029">How high off the ground is the launchpad from which the rocket lifts off?</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00031">0 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00032">2 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00033">8 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00034">15 feet</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00035">Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">The correct answer is 8 feet.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0750a278-9b95-4e76-9997-19b7297b90d3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00037">Use the following scenario to answer questions 5 – 8.</para>
          <para id="para-00038"><quote id="quote-00002">The expressions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> define the same function. The function models the number of lumens emitted by a spotlight in an art exhibit over the course of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds.</quote></para>
          <para id="para-00039">Which equation represents the time when the spotlight is not emitting any light?</para>
          <para id="para-00040">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>675</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00045">Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00046">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>90</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e5fc91a9-34b4-455f-b981-0837a3479e43" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00047">At what time(s) does the spotlight not emit any light?</para>
          <para id="para-00048">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00049">0 and 30 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00050">10 and 25 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00051">Only 0 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00052">15 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00053">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is 0 and 30 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3ce1ef69-1b98-4969-acd5-c48e61d1d1f3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00055">The artist planned for the spotlight to emit 600 lumens at 10 seconds from the start. At what other time will the spotlight emit 600 lumens of light?</para>
          <para id="para-00056">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00057">0 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00058">20 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00059">25 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00060">30 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00061">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is 20 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_34dd878a-a1d9-490a-bcfe-161061de6d55" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00063">At 5 seconds, the spotlight will emit 375 lumens. Find another time that the spotlight emits 375 lumens.</para>
          <para id="para-00064">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00065">0 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00066">10 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00067">15 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00068">25 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00069">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00070">The correct answer is 25 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d1aa4d5f-093f-4b11-90d5-d40945962b23" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00071">9-10.</para>
          <para id="para-00072"><quote id="quote-00003">A bowling alley models the revenue from sales in one day as a function of the cost to rent a lane per hour, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Here are two expressions defining the same revenue function.</quote><quote id="quote-00004"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></quote><quote id="quote-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></quote></para>
          <para id="para-00073">According to this model, how high would the cost to rent a lane have to be for the bowling alley to make $0 in revenue?</para>
          <para id="para-00074">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00075">$8</para>
          <para id="para-00076">$10</para>
          <para id="para-00077">$14</para>
          <para id="para-00078">$16</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00079">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00080">The correct answer is $16.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_71966d95-aaa8-45f2-8ea8-abb97354839d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00081">What equation can you write to determine the lane cost that would allow the bowling alley to make $640 in revenue?</para>
          <para id="para-00082">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>640</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>640</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00087">Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00088">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>160</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>640</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>